<header class="page-hero"><div class="shell"><div class="eyebrow">About XGL</div><h1>Built by people who know what it means to stand behind the work.</h1><p>Expedition Growth Lab exists to help strong independent companies grow without becoming generic, brittle, over-financialized versions of themselves.</p></div></header><main><section class="section alt"><div class="shell grid2"><div><div class="kicker">Provenance</div><h2 class="section-title">The business world looks different from underneath the machine.</h2></div><div class="bodycopy"><p>Brian Reymore’s background includes nearly two decades in the RV industry doing repair, fabrication, custom builds and remodels, along with logistics, transportation, trucking, warehousing, dock supervision, retail, sales, management, customer service, and entrepreneurship.</p><p>That history became the lens for XGL: systems are only useful when they survive contact with the people doing the work.</p></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="shell grid2"><div class="quote"><p>“XGL was built by people who know what it’s like to make, move, repair, sell and stand behind real things.”</p></div><div><div class="kicker">The operating belief</div><h2 class="section-title">Protect first. Grow second.</h2><div class="bodycopy"><p>Scale is not automatically success. Growth that destroys craftsmanship, founder judgment, employee dignity, customer trust, or independence is just a bigger problem.</p><p>XGL’s job is to help good builders become more capable while preserving the human reasons they were worth rooting for in the first place.</p></div></div></div></section></main><footer class="footer"><div class="shell"><span>Expedition Growth Lab LLC · Oregon</span><span>Protect the Build. Grow the Legacy.</span><div class="footer-links"><a href="/contact">Contact</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="/terms">Terms</a></div></div></footer></body></html>